Hosting and auto-deploy


🚀 Run Locally
The app lives inside the p folder.

# 1. Clone the repository
git clone <your-repo-url>

# 2. Go into the app folder
cd <repo-folder>/p

# 3. Install dependencies
npm install

# 4. Start the dev server
npm run dev

Then open http://localhost:5173 in your browser.

📦 Build for production 

npm run build

The output goes to the dist folder.

📁 Project Structure
Click to expand 

p/
├── public/
│   └── music.mp3              # background music
├── src/
│   ├── assets/images/         # photos used in the story
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── Navbar.jsx
│   │   ├── FloatingElements.jsx
│   │   ├── Frame.jsx          # photo + message card (Previous / Next)
│   │   ├── Question.jsx
│   │   ├── FinalScreen.jsx
│   │   ├── DiwaliScreen.jsx   # Diwali blessing
│   │   ├── AnarScreen.jsx     # anar and fireworks scene
│   │   └── MusicPlayer.jsx
│   ├── data/story.js          # images and messages for each frame
│   ├── App.jsx                # controls the flow between screens
│   └── main.jsx
└── package.json

✏️ Customize
I want to change...
Edit this
📸 Photos and messages
src/data/story.js and src/assets/images/
🎶 Music
Replace public/music.mp3
🪔 Diwali wishes
The lines list in src/components/DiwaliScreen.jsx
⏱️ Pause between wishes
GAP in DiwaliScreen.jsx
🎇 When the anar lights
IGNITE in AnarScreen.jsx


🌐 Deployment
Deployed on Netlify from this repository. Every push to the main branch redeploys the site automatically.

Setting
Value
Base directory
p
Build command
npm run build
Publish directory
dist


📝 Good to Know
🔊 Browsers block audio until the visitor interacts with the page, so the music starts on the first tap or click.
📱 Works on phones and laptops. Landscape or desktop gives the best view of the Diwali scenes.

